<Legal title="Data processing agreement" slug="dpa" updated="2026-11-13" description={`The agreement that covers personal data ${brand} handles for your company: roles, security, subprocessors, deletion and audits.`}>
<p>An owner accepts this agreement for the company in the portal, under Data, then Data processing agreement. The portal records who accepted, for which company, and when.</p>
<h2>1. Who is who</h2><p>Your company (the "controller") decides why and how personal data is used. [Company legal name] ("{brand}", the "processor") handles that data only to provide the service, and only on your documented instructions: this agreement, the <a href="/legal/terms">terms of service</a>, and the settings you choose in the portal.</p>
<h2>2. What is processed</h2><ul><li><strong>People:</strong> your team members, guests you invite, and people whose details your team enters into apps (for example your customers).</li><li><strong>Data:</strong> names, email addresses, roles, sign-in records, and the content your team puts into the portal and the apps you install.</li><li><strong>How long:</strong> while your organization exists, for the periods you set under Data, then Retention. After an organization is deleted, its data is removed within 30 days and leaves backups within [N] days.</li></ul>
<h2>3. What {brand} commits to</h2><ul><li>Use the data only to provide the service. It is not sold and is not used to train AI models. Apps may use content to improve their AI features only when you turn that on under Data.</li><li>Keep it confidential: only people who need access to run or support the service have it, and they are bound to confidentiality.</li><li>Protect it as described on the <a href="/security">security page</a>: encryption in transit and at rest, separation between organizations, access logs and backups.</li><li>Help you answer requests from people about their data, and tell you without delay if a person or an authority contacts {brand} directly about your data, unless the law forbids it.</li><li>Tell you without undue delay, and within 72 hours of becoming aware, about a personal data breach that affects your organization, with what is known and what is being done.</li><li>Give you the information you reasonably need to show compliance, and allow an audit once a year on 30 days' notice, at your cost, in a way that does not expose other customers' data.</li></ul>
<h2>4. Subprocessors</h2><p>{brand} uses the companies on the <a href="/legal/subprocessors">subprocessors page</a> and holds each to obligations no weaker than these. That page is updated at least 30 days before a new subprocessor starts. If you object on reasonable grounds within that time and no solution is found, you may end the affected service and receive a refund for the unused prepaid period.</p>
<p>Third-party apps you install from the catalog are chosen by you and are not subprocessors of {brand}. Each app receives only the access you approve, and its developer's own terms apply.</p>
<h2>5. Where data is kept</h2><p>Your organization's data is stored in the region shown in the portal under Data. If personal data is transferred outside the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom to a country without an adequacy decision, the EU Standard Contractual Clauses (and the UK Addendum where it applies) form part of this agreement.</p>
<h2>6. When the service ends</h2><p>You can export your data at any time. When your organization is deleted, {brand} deletes its data as set out in section 2, except what the law requires to be kept, such as billing records.</p>
<h2>7. Liability and order</h2><p>The limits of liability in the terms of service apply to this agreement. Where this agreement and the terms say different things about personal data, this agreement decides.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2><p>[Company legal name], [registered address]. Questions about this agreement: <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
